# Reader / Writer

- **Reader:** external UI definition file → `RawDefinition`.
- **Writer:** `RawDefinition` → external UI definition file (create/overwrite).
- Isolate all external-format parsing/serialization here (and under `io/formats/` when a second format appears — YAGNI until then).
- Do not import `UIDefinition` from Reader/Writer; go through Raw + Transformer.
- Raw must remain independent of Reader/Writer (no reverse dependency).
- Optional IR **lineage** keys on Raw (`basedOn`, `changeReason`, …) are not vendor vocabulary. Writers may embed them in artifact comments when the target dialect allows. Import must not invent `basedOn` from a vendor file.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const raw = await reader.read(path);
// validate → transform elsewhere

// ❌ BAD
const ir = await reader.readAsIR(path);
```
